@lifecycle-status @read-only @manual-workflow
Feature: Lifecycle status for active SDLC work
  As a developer using the manual nmg-sdlc workflow
  I want a concise lifecycle-status command that infers the active context and next action
  So that I can recover work without manually inspecting scattered artifacts

  Scenario: Infer the current manual SDLC stage from consistent evidence
    Given a repository is on an issue branch with a complete matching spec package
    And no implementation, verification, or pull request evidence exists
    When the developer runs the lifecycle-status command
    Then the status reports the issue, branch, and "specified" lifecycle stage
    And the completed artifacts include the issue branch and spec package
    And the missing artifacts include implementation, verification, and pull request
    And the next action is "$nmg-sdlc:write-code" for the inferred issue

  Scenario: Preserve dirty work and local artifacts
    Given the repository contains dirty user changes
    When the developer runs the lifecycle-status command in text and JSON modes
    Then both outputs report the dirty condition
    And no file, git ref, branch, issue, pull request, project status, or process is changed
    And a repeated invocation over unchanged evidence produces the same lifecycle conclusion

  Scenario: Degrade safely when optional evidence is unavailable
    Given the repository has enough local evidence to identify an issue branch
    And optional spec, verification, pull request, CI, or GitHub evidence is absent, stale, or unavailable
    When the developer runs the lifecycle-status command
    Then available evidence still appears in the result
    And unavailable facts are labelled unknown and material gaps are listed
    And the reported stage does not advance beyond the strongest consistent evidence
    And a stale passing report remains not current while its report commit stays visible as provenance

  Scenario: Produce status without prompting or acting
    Given a repository has any supported manual lifecycle state
    When the lifecycle-status command evaluates its evidence
    Then it produces a lifecycle stage and evidence-based next action without prompting
    And it does not execute the recommended action

  Scenario: Emit stable machine-readable status
    Given a caller requests machine-readable lifecycle status
    When the lifecycle-status command completes with successful and recoverably failed probes
    Then stdout contains valid JSON with schemaVersion 1
    And the JSON contains project, issue, spec, verification, pullRequest, stage, completedArtifacts, missingArtifacts, gaps, and nextAction fields
    And diagnostic prose does not corrupt the JSON stream

  @out-of-scope
  Scenario: Exclude automated-runner integration ahead of milestone-2 removal
    Given the automated SDLC runner is scheduled for removal in milestone 2
    When lifecycle status is implemented for issue 145
    Then it does not read runner state, sentinels, logs, configuration, or PIDs
    And it does not modify runner source or tests
    And it does not recommend runner resume, cleanup, or end-loop actions
